  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Fix half-up percentage rounding in invoice totals",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "## Objective\ninvoiceTotal must return 1835 for one item at 1999 cents, quantity 1, 15% discount, 8% tax.\n\n## Findings so far\n- Reproduced: current code returns 1836.\n- src/money.js percentOf uses Math.floor, which truncates instead of rounding half up. Discount 15% of 1999 = 299.85 -> should be 300, code gives 299; net becomes 1700 instead of 1699 and 8% tax then compounds the error.\n\n## Work\n- Implement round-half-up-to-the-cent rounding in src/money.js (integer-safe, no floating point drift).\n- Keep pricing.js and tax.js using the shared helper so all percentage amounts follow the same rule.\n- Add tests: the reported order (1835), a discount-only case, a tax-only half case, and a zero percent case.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- c1 reported order returns 1835.\n- c2 percentage amounts round to nearest cent, halves up.\n- c3 root cause fixed in the shared money helper, no special-casing in invoice.js.\n- c4 npm test passes.\n- Independent reviewer (not the implementer) confirms the cause and the fix against the files.",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
